\tr{\td{1}\td{224.05}\td{11.65}\td{212.21}\td{208.34}\td{}\td{1}\td{1}}
\tr{\td{2}\td{113.40}\td{11.77}\td{101.39}\td{104.89}\td{}\td{2.09}\td{1.99}}
\tr{\td{4}\td{64.58}\td{11.92}\td{52.66}\td{55.49}\td{53.28}\td{4.03}\td{3.75}}
\tr{\td{8}\td{42.63}\td{12.06}\td{30.57}\td{38.06}\td{28.74}\td{6.94}\td{5.47}}
}

\p{(One worker, batch: the worker drives the environment pass itself, 2.2 s of the 212.2 s. Peak RSS 2.7 GB with one worker, 3.6 GB batch / 4.0 GB pipelined with 8.)}

\p{Where \code{\verb~|workers x check wall~} goes:}

\table{
\tr{\th{workers}\th{mode}\th{worker CPU}\th{on a CPU}\th{run queue}\th{stopped (collections, faults)}\th{parked at the frontier}\th{parked, tail}\th{environment thread CPU}\th{collections in the check phase}}
\tr{\td{1}\td{batch}\td{212.2 s}\td{100.0 \%}\td{0.0 \%}\td{0.0 \%}\td{0.0 \%}\td{0.0 \%}\td{(in the worker)}\td{295 / 0.97 s}}
\tr{\td{1}\td{pipelined}\td{207.4 s}\td{99.7 \%}\td{0.0 \%}\td{0.3 \%}\td{0.0 \%}\td{0.0 \%}\td{2.91 s}\td{407 / 1.81 s}}
\tr{\td{2}\td{batch}\td{201.2 s}\td{99.2 \%}\td{0.0 \%}\td{0.7 \%}\td{0.1 \%}\td{0.0 \%}\td{4.56 s}\td{312 / 1.04 s}}
\tr{\td{2}\td{pipelined}\td{206.1 s}\td{98.5 \%}\td{0.0 \%}\td{1.5 \%}\td{0.0 \%}\td{0.0 \%}\td{2.97 s}\td{368 / 2.07 s}}
\tr{\td{4}\td{batch}\td{204.8 s}\td{97.2 \%}\td{0.4 \%}\td{2.0 \%}\td{0.2 \%}\td{0.1 \%}\td{4.58 s}\td{245 / 1.01 s}}
\tr{\td{4}\td{pipelined}\td{210.8 s}\td{95.5 \%}\td{0.0 \%}\td{4.5 \%}\td{0.0 \%}\td{0.0 \%}\td{3.03 s}\td{384 / 2.54 s}}
\tr{\td{8}\td{batch}\td{212.7 s}\td{87.0 \%}\td{7.5 \%}\td{4.4 \%}\td{0.7 \%}\td{0.4 \%}\td{4.85 s}\td{194 / 1.06 s}}
\tr{\td{8}\td{pipelined}\td{224.0 s}\td{74.5 \%}\td{13.6 \%}\td{11.6 \%}\td{0.1 \%}\td{0.3 \%}\td{3.33 s}\td{398 / 3.87 s}}
}

\p{Reading:}

\ul{
\li{\strong{Collections are the serial part.} The pause time per check pass is the same at every worker count (about 1 s; 1.8 s - 3.9 s with the pipelined loader's garbage on top), so its share of the wall clock is 0.5 \% with one worker and 3.5 \% (batch) / 10.3 \% (pipelined) with 8. A check pass frees 14 GB (20 KB per unit, 1 MB per session reset) whatever the worker count; the pipelined run frees 35.6 GB.}
\li{\strong{Run queue.} Batch, 8 workers: 7.5 \% = the environment thread (4.85 s of CPU during the first 6.3 s) + about 5 \% of host noise. Pipelined: loader + environment thread + 8 workers on 8 cores for 21.65 s (the load alone takes 12.06 s): 13.6 \%.}
\li{\strong{The workers never wait for the loader or the frontier}: loaded 334,030 units at 10 s, announced 333,268, accepted 204,673; parks 0.1 \%. Environment thread: 2.3 s inside the pass + 4.0 s adding up \code{\verb~|Store.sharedBytes()~} after each of its 12,744 steps (\code{\verb~|DeclTable.claimBytes~} walks one slot per unit: 0.3 ms): a driver bug, fixed (section 6).}
\li{\strong{No unit and no chain bounds Mathlib}: slowest unit 2.15 s (376698, a declined unit re-checked by the reference kernel), then 0.74 s; the heaviest unit holds 0.2 \% of the machine's steps; the work is spread evenly along the file (10 \% of the steps in the first 12.8 \% of the units, 90 \% in the first 86.8 \%); "frontier complete" to "last unit checked" is simply the rest of the run, and the tail proper is 0.1 - 0.25 s per worker.}
\li{\strong{Worker CPU}: 201 s with 2 workers, 205 s with 4, 213 s with 8 (batch); pipelined 206 / 211 / 224 s. Eight one-worker processes over eight shards use the same 210 - 213 s (section 5): the growth is the hardware's (eight busy cores), not the process's.}
}
}

