\p{The warm JVM checks Mathlib in 23.6 s with 8 workers against 28.7 s for the image (C2's code is 17 \% faster in worker CPU); cold it is as fast as the image. Its 1 GB young generation makes collections rare in a check pass (1.5 \%), but with the pipelined loader each young collection copies what the loader just made (50 - 100 ms): 7 \%. Peak RSS 6.3 GB (batch, two passes) and 11.2 GB (pipelined): the heap setting, not the need.}
}

